# UTF-8 file encoding (Windows)

All text/source files must be **UTF-8 without BOM**. UTF-16 breaks `dotnet build` and wastes tokens.

## Proven behavior (Windows)

| Method | Encoding |
|--------|----------|
| Cursor `Write` | **UTF-16 — never use for text files** |
| Cursor `StrReplace` | UTF-8 (edits to existing UTF-8 files only) |
| Shell `WriteAllText` + `UTF8Encoding(false)` | UTF-8 (new files) |

## Mandatory workflow

1. **Edits:** `StrReplace` on existing UTF-8 files only.
2. **New files:** shell only — **never** Cursor `Write`:
   ```powershell
   $utf8 = New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding $false
   [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText('<path>', @'
   <content>
   '@, $utf8)
   ```
   Or: `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/encoding/WriteUtf8.ps1 -Path <path> -Content '<content>'`
3. **Never** use PowerShell defaults: `Out-File`, bare `Set-Content`, `>` / `>>` redirection.

## Enforcement

- `dotnet run --project tools/HarnessSync -- --check` fails on UTF-16 text files.
- Optional pre-commit: `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`

## Recovery (legacy corruption only)

If a file is already UTF-16: `tools/encoding/Repair-TextFileUtf8.ps1` — not part of normal create flow.